@@Zortex release
@@Roadmap
@P
@size(epic)

Goal: someone who has never seen zortex can install the plugin, take notes
for a week, and (optionally) run the server, without reading the source or
hitting a personal default. Ship as v0.1.0; everything under # 4 waits.
What is done is in ../CHANGELOG.md; what was decided and why, in
Wishlist.md (sections 8 and 9).

**Definition of done:**
- [ ] A tagged release with `zortex` binaries and a container image @p1 @size(sm)

# 6 Proposed (review of 2026-10-16)
From a review of what a new user meets first. Done since: `:ZortexRename`
shows what it changes and asks, Markdown and Obsidian import
(`:ZortexImportMarkdown`), backups and the format promise in the README,
and Neovim's edits to notes that aren't open are checked like the web
app's.

## 6.1 Before the tag
- [ ] Use `release-prep` on a real vault for about a week before tagging v0.1.0: many features landed on 2026-10-16 and 2026-10-22 without real notes behind them @p1 @size(sm)
- [ ] `m` (inbox triage) and `:ZortexMove` show what they will change and ask first, as `:ZortexRename` does, when they write notes that aren't open @p1 @size(sm)
- [ ] One command that checks a vault: long labels, broken links, tags that go nowhere, task ids that don't line up, conflict copies, the problems the calendar note flags (repeating rules), and state files older versions left in `.z/` @p2 @size(sm)
- [ ] A shorter README: the pitch, the screenshot, the quickstart and a feature list; the generated command and key tables live in `:help` and the docs @p2 @size(sm)

## 6.2 Workflow
- [ ] Capture from the phone's share menu: the installed web app as a share target (a link or text lands in the inbox; inbox adds already wait offline until the server is back) @p2 @size(md)
- [ ] Undo on the web: a "ticked · undo" toast for a few seconds after ticking or deleting a line @p2 @size(sm)

## 6.3 Later
- [ ] The web area overview (Wishlist # 2) @p3 @size(md)
- [ ] Windows: try it, and say what works @p3 @size(md)

# 7 Proposed (review of 2026-10-22)
From a review before publishing. Not agreed item by item yet.

## 7.1 Before the tag
- [ ] `@from(date) @to(date)` on a day's line (a span of days) works in Neovim only, the web app doesn't show it: drop it, or port it to Go with fixtures (`@repeat` under a day is gone: rules live in `# Repeating`) @p2 @size(sm)
- [ ] Issue templates: a bug report asks for the version, `:checkhealth zortex` and the lines involved; a format question points at Syntax.md @p3 @size(xs)

## 7.2 Workflow
- [ ] Note conflict copies: `:ZortexConflicts` opens each `*.sync-conflict-*` note beside its note as a diff and deletes it once merged (`:checkhealth` only lists them today; state files in `.z/` merge themselves) @p2 @size(sm)
- [ ] Quick capture in Neovim: `:ZortexCapture text` adds a line to the inbox without opening it (Wishlist # 3) @p3 @size(xs)

# 4 After v0.1.0
- [ ] Tree-sitter grammar with the AST fixtures as acceptance tests (Wishlist # 7) @size(xl)

Dropped: a raw-text section, uploading a file to render it, tags generated from Structure, other rules for a tagged heading's rows, XP "overlap", the calendar picker, a `|` alias in links (it breaks table rows).

Decisions:
- One repo, one version: the plugin and `zortex serve` are tagged together (decided 2026-10-16).
- Platforms promised: Linux and macOS; Windows untested (README, decided 2026-10-14).
- Names: `zortex.nvim` for the plugin, `zortex` for the binary and the image on ghcr.io (`ghcr.io/t-wilkinson/zortex`, decided 2026-10-16).
- Notifications: every timed calendar line notifies (keeps you on track, pulls you out of deep focus); `@n(no)` opts a line out, `@event` marks the fixed things you plan around (decided 2026-10-16).
- Versioning: semver; `CHANGELOG.md` is the record of what changed (decided 2026-10-13).
- Display text: `[text](link)`, Markdown's form; URLs and files in parentheses stay Markdown links (decided 2026-10-22).
- Repeating rules are bounded by `@from(date)` and `@to(date)` (decided 2026-10-22).
- Two devices never write the same synced file: `.z/` holds shared, rarely changed state; the rest stays per machine (decided 2026-10-22).
